@prefix execution: <http://example.org/orexis/execution#> .
@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix onboarding: <http://example.org/orexis/onboarding#> .

<> a onboarding:RequirementGraph .    # this document is one graph, and this is what it is

#  WHAT A WORLD MUST STATE OF execution's WORDS, held by onboarding alone before anything is granted
#  (knowledge/domain/onboarding/requirement.md, #838). No agent loads this graph: its kind is
#  onboarding's, and the boot passes over it as it passes over a world's hardware.

#  AN EXECUTOR'S FIGURES, ONE EACH, on whichever role states them: a domain's role beneath the executor may, so each
#  shape targets what states the figure. The executor reads them in one query as it is made and judges nothing of
#  them, this being where they are judged; that two roles do not state two values of one figure is onboarding's
#  own requirement, of every package's figures.
[] a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetSubjectsOf execution:patienceS ;
    sh:property [ sh:path execution:patienceS ; sh:maxCount 1 ; sh:minExclusive 0 ;
                  sh:message "an executor's patience is one number of seconds above nought" ] .
